## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement cost-aware, latency-conscious routing in a simple, auditable way. Focuses on per-tenant accounting, model pricing, and practical test coverage.

## Key Concepts

- Cost-aware routing and SLA mapping
- Per-tenant ledger and budget enforcement
- Simple fallback behaviors and test plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: ledger update and routing decision
function routePrompt(tenant, prompt) {
  const remaining = tenant.budget - tenant.spent;
  for (const m of ['fast','balanced','accurate']) {
    if (cost(m, prompt) <= remaining && latency(m, prompt) <= tenant.sla[m]) {
      tenant.spent += cost(m, prompt);
      return m;
    }
  }
  return 'cached';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to handle budget rollovers and monthly resets?
- How would you test this with A/B experiments across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ability to design per-tenant budgets with latency guarantees, bursts, and data locality in a production-grade LLM gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Token bucket and backpressure
- Budget drift detection and alerting
- Regional data locality and routing
- Canary routing and model variant selection based on budget state

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal per-tenant token bucket (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate; this.capacity = capacity; this.tokens = capacity; this.last = Date.now();
  }
  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const add = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + add);
    this.last = now;
  }
  consume(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate budgets against real traffic with drift scenarios?
- What observability would you add to detect bursts without SLA violations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design real-time, scalable guardrails spanning telemetry, model routing, and incident response in multi-tenant LLM gateways, a common production pain point.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming telemetry and per-tenant baselines
- Anomaly scoring combining statistical and rule-based signals
- Remediation policies: throttle, safe-model routing, quarantine
- Auditability and drift handling across tenants
- Data locality and privacy impacts

## Code Example
```javascript
function score(latency, tokens, entropy, baseline) {
  const zLat = (latency - baseline.latency.mean) / baseline.latency.std;
  const zTok = (tokens - baseline.tokens.mean) / baseline.tokens.std;
  const zEnt = (entropy - baseline.entropy.mean) / baseline.entropy.std;
  return Math.max(0, Math.abs(zLat) + Math.abs(zTok) + Math.abs(zEnt));
}
```

